// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2999776523" "Hrm. So the experiment was a success, but there is an unknown component that is tainting our data. An interesting turn of events, {HeroName}, but not unexpected.<br><br>The Infected are too promising to leave be. The chemicals from the Arachnoids, if perfected, could instantly give <i>anyone</i> super powers. Even if left unperfected, having control over the Infected could give one an army of followers on <i>demand</i>.<br><br>I believe Arachnos will have great use for this, and they would pay me handsomly for this. However... I think you and I would make <i>much</i> better use of these dregs than Arachnos, don't you agree?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P468861657" "<color orange>The supposed leader of the Infected looks straight into your eyes.</color><br><br>The Calling. All who have been Infected, gather towards me.<br><br>I shall bring you to the Promised Land, where we will find the cure to our condition. Abandon the urge to drink more from the water, focus on my will!"
// Answer Text :
"P1550217068" "(Examine the leader closer)"
// Page Examine Text :
"P3628362497" "<color orange>Upon closer examination, you're able to tell that someone else is controlling this Infected. It seems to be some sort of telepathy!<br><br>Whoever is doing this is trying to bring the Infected somewhere to <i>cure</i> them of their condition. There can only be one group who would try such a thing - Longbow!</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P2395377593" "Longbow. Always getting in the way."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1564468460" "We cannot have someone else controlling these Infected. I suspect it is either a rival scientist or Longbow. If the latter, then we <i>must</i> stop them.<br><br>They will seek to try to cure the Infected, to make them <i>normal</i> again. How horrible would that be? To have your life altered, your purpose <i>bettered</i>, only for you to return to your banal existence as some... <i>dreg</i> living in a slum.<br><br>We can find who is doing this, {HeroName}. It is our <i>duty</i> towards our own destinies and the destinies of these people to do so."
// AcceptString :
"P952263822" "Do you have any idea of where to look?"
// SendOffString :
"P4267913364" "I just might. There are reports of other Infected murmuring about some 'calling' in Mercy City.<br><br>I believe the use of brute force is necessary with this. If you can find and defeat enough of them, I will use my devices to try to locate where this supposed 'calling' for them is coming from.<br><br>I will send you a message when I've found the location."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3995709868" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: The Infected Solution</color>"

